{
  "_README": [
    "TEMPLATE 4 of 4 — REPEATABLE INDUSTRY PAGE  (/industries-served/healthcare)",
    "",
    "This is the pattern for all 8 industry pages. To adapt it, change the Service node, the",
    "audience, the compliance block, the image, the WebPage, the breadcrumb leaf, and the FAQ.",
    "",
    "THE CENTRAL IDEA — this is the answer to your question about expressing that healthcare",
    "gets a heightened HIPAA/HITECH focus you would not apply elsewhere:",
    "",
    "An industry page is NOT a different service. It is the SAME service delivered to a",
    "narrowed audience under a specific regulatory regime. Model it that way and the",
    "differentiation becomes machine-readable:",
    "",
    "  isSimilarTo / isRelatedTo  -> links back to the core service pages, so Google understands",
    "                                this is healthcare-flavoured data destruction, not a",
    "                                separate unrelated offering",
    "  audience: MedicalAudience  -> the narrowing. MedicalAudience is a real schema.org type and",
    "                                is far more specific than the generic Audience your live",
    "                                markup uses",
    "  about: DefinedTerm HIPAA   -> the regulatory regime as an ENTITY with an authoritative",
    "         + HITECH               hhs.gov URL, not a keyword string",
    "  additionalProperty         -> the concrete obligations you meet",
    "",
    "The equivalent blocks on your other industry pages carry FERPA, GLBA, FISMA and so on.",
    "Same shape, different regime. That is what tells Google these are genuinely distinct pages",
    "rather than eight near-duplicates of one service page.",
    "",
    "WHAT THIS FIXES vs your live markup",
    "  1. provider stub with a cross-page @id — same fix as template 3.",
    "  2. audience was a generic Audience with a prose string. Now MedicalAudience.",
    "  3. Zero compliance signals in the structured data, despite HIPAA appearing 11 times and",
    "     HITECH 3 times in the visible copy. The page says it; the markup did not.",
    "  4. No image. Hero at industries-healthcare-hero.png was undeclared.",
    "  5. areaServed was plain strings.",
    "  6. No link between this page and the underlying service pages.",
    "",
    "RICH RESULT ELIGIBILITY: Breadcrumbs.",
    "Strip all _README and _comment keys before shipping."
  ],

